  "Goals": [
    "Critique (in writing) a strategy using the Pythagorean Identity for identifying the value of sine and tangent from the known value of cosine and the quadrant of the angle.",
    "Use the Pythagorean Identity to determine the value of all 3 trigonometric ratios given the value of 1 to start from and the quadrant of the angle."
  ],
  "ElementCount": 52,
  "SourceElements": [
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L06-ACTIVITY-001",
      "SourceSection": "6.1: Math Talk: Which Quadrant?",
      "SourceExcerpt": "For an angle \\(\\theta\\) in the quadrant indicated, use mental estimation to identify the values of \\(\\cos(\\theta)\\), \\(\\sin(\\theta)\\), and \\(\\tan(\\theta)\\) as either positive or negative.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L06-ACTIVITY-002",
      "SourceSection": "6.2: Andre's Calculations",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Suppose that the angle \\(\\theta\\), in radians, is in quadrant 4 of the unit circle. If \\(\\cos(\\theta)=0.28\\), what are the values of \\(\\sin(\\theta)\\) and \\(\\tan(\\theta)\\)?",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L06-ACTIVITY-003",
      "SourceSection": "6.2: Andre's Calculations",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Andre uses the Pythagorean Identity and determines that the value of \\(\\sin(\\theta)\\) is -0.96. Using the values of sine and cosine, he then calculates the value of tangent:",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L06-ACTIVITY-004",
      "SourceSection": "6.2: Andre's Calculations",
      "SourceExcerpt": "\\(\\begin{align} \\tan(\\theta)&=\\dfrac{\\sin(\\theta)}{\\cos(\\theta)} \\\\ &=\\frac{\\text-0.96}{0.28} \\\\ &\\approx \\text-3.43 \\end{align}\\)",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L06-ACTIVITY-005",
      "SourceSection": "6.2: Andre's Calculations",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Do you agree with Andre? Explain or show your reasoning.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L06-ACTIVITY-006",
      "SourceSection": "6.3: Card Sort: Where's the Point?",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Your teacher will give you a set of cards that should be arranged face up with cards showing values for sine, cosine, and tangent on one side and cards showing quadrants on the other.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L06-ACTIVITY-007",
      "SourceSection": "6.3: Card Sort: Where's the Point?",
      "SourceExcerpt": "For each pair, explain to your partner how you know if the pair is or is not possible on the unit circle. Once a pair is identified, place the cards in front of you to use later.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L06-ACTIVITY-008",
      "SourceSection": "6.3: Card Sort: Where's the Point?",
      "SourceExcerpt": "For each pair that your partner draws, listen carefully to their explanation. If you disagree, discuss your thinking and work to reach an agreement.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L06-ACTIVITY-009",
      "SourceSection": "6.3: Card Sort: Where's the Point?",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Take turns with your partner matching pairs of cards. Identify 2 pairs that are possible on the unit circle and 2 pairs that are not possible, in any order.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L06-ACTIVITY-010",
      "SourceSection": "6.3: Card Sort: Where's the Point?",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Once you and your partner have identified 4 pairs each, pick 1 of your possible matches and then calculate the values of the two missing trigonometric ratios for that match. When you finish, trade calculations with your partner and check…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L06-ACTIVITY-011",
      "SourceSection": "6.3: Card Sort: Where's the Point?",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Suppose \\(\\tan(\\theta)=2\\) and the angle \\(\\theta\\) is in quadrant 1. Find the values of \\(\\cos(\\theta)\\) and \\(\\sin(\\theta)\\).",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L06-ACTIVITY-012",
      "SourceSection": "6.3: Card Sort: Where's the Point?",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Say we know that \\(\\sin(\\theta)=\\text-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\) and that \\(\\theta\\) is an angle in quadrant 3. What can we say about the values of cosine and tangent at \\(\\theta\\)?",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L06-ACTIVITY-013",
      "SourceSection": "6.3: Card Sort: Where's the Point?",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Since we can think of \\(\\sin(\\theta)\\) as the \\(y\\)-coordinate of a point \\(P\\) in quadrant 3, let’s start with a sketch of the unit circle showing point \\(P\\).",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L06-ACTIVITY-014",
      "SourceSection": "6.3: Card Sort: Where's the Point?",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The sketch helps us see that the \\(x\\)-coordinate, which is \\(\\cos(\\theta)\\), is also negative. Using the Pythagorean Identity, we can calculate the value of \\(\\cos(\\theta)\\):",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L06-ACTIVITY-015",
      "SourceSection": "6.3: Card Sort: Where's the Point?",
      "SourceExcerpt": "\\(\\begin{align} \\cos^2(\\theta)+\\sin^2(\\theta)&=1^2 \\\\ \\cos^2(\\theta)+\\left(\\text-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)^2 &= 1 \\\\ \\cos^2(\\theta)&=1-\\left(\\text-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)^2 \\\\ \\cos^2(\\theta)&=1-\\frac{2}{4} \\\\…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L06-ACTIVITY-016",
      "SourceSection": "6.3: Card Sort: Where's the Point?",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Now that we know the value of cosine, we can calculate the value of tangent with some division:",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L06-ACTIVITY-017",
      "SourceSection": "6.3: Card Sort: Where's the Point?",
      "SourceExcerpt": "\\(\\tan(\\theta)=\\dfrac{\\text-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}}{\\text-\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}}}=\\dfrac{\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}}{\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}}=1\\)",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L06-ACTIVITY-018",
      "SourceSection": "6.3: Card Sort: Where's the Point?",
      "SourceExcerpt": "We can use one piece of information and the structure of the unit circle to figure out a whole bunch more, similar to how we used the value of one side length, the hypotenuse, and the structure of right triangles in the past to figure out…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L06-ACTIVITY-019",
      "SourceSection": "6.3: Card Sort: Where's the Point?",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The identity \\(\\sin^2(x) + \\cos^2(x) = 1\\) relating the sine and cosine of a number. It is called the Pythagorean identity because it follows from the Pythagorean theorem.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L06-ACTIVITY-020",
      "SourceSection": "6.3: Card Sort: Where's the Point?",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Pythagorean identity",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L06-ACTIVITY-021",
      "SourceSection": "6.3: Card Sort: Where's the Point?",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The length of an interval at which a periodic function repeats. A function \\(f\\) has a period, \\(p\\), if \\(f(x+p) = f(x)\\) for all inputs \\(x\\).",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L06-ACTIVITY-022",
      "SourceSection": "6.3: Card Sort: Where's the Point?",
      "SourceExcerpt": "A function whose values repeat at regular intervals. If \\(f\\) is a periodic function then there is a number \\(p\\), called the period, so that \\(f(x + p) = f(x)\\) for all inputs \\(x\\).",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L06-ACTIVITY-023",
      "SourceSection": "6.3: Card Sort: Where's the Point?",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The circle in the coordinate plane with radius 1 and center the origin.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
